---
description: Use TypeStyles recipes and design tokens for UI chrome, not plain CSS files.
alwaysApply: true
---

# TypeStyles first

Var UI styles first-party UI with TypeStyles recipes, not new `*.css` files.

- Tokens: `designTokens` (`t.space`, `t.color`, …)
- Breakpoints: `breakpoint('md', 'max')` — never raw `@media (max-width: …)` for design breakpoints
- Apply classes with `mergeProps` / `combine` from `typestyles` (re-exported by `@var-ui/astro` / `@var-ui/react`)
- Register site/kit recipes in the TypeStyles extract entry (`docs/src/styles/index.ts`, `@var-ui/docs/styles`)

```ts
// ❌ BAD — chrome in a CSS file
.foo { gap: 0.75rem; }
@media (max-width: 767px) { .foo { display: none; } }

// ✅ GOOD — recipe + tokens
export const foo = typestyles.recipe('docs-foo', () => ({
  slots: ['root'],
  root: {
    gap: t.space[3].var,
    [breakpoint('md', 'max')]: { display: 'none' },
  },
}), { layer: 'components' });
```

Plain CSS is only for third-party/uncontrolled markup, or when TypeStyles cannot express the rule.
